,{},"vld::schema::parse_coerced",", which repairs two common mismatches and retries:",[1274,1741,1742,1762],{},[1277,1743,1744,1745,1747,1748,1751,1752,1515,1755,818,1758,1761],{},"a field whose schema expects a ",[1196,1746,1732],{}," but got a coerced number or boolean gets its original text back — ",[393,1749,1750],{},"?q=123"," into ",[393,1753,1754],{},"vld::string()",[393,1756,1757],{},"\"123\"",[393,1759,1760],{},"?zip=01234"," was never converted in the first place;",[1277,1763,1764,1765,1768,1769,1751,1772,1515,1775,1151],{},"a field whose schema expects an ",[1196,1766,1767],{},"array"," but got a single value is wrapped — ",[393,1770,1771],{},"?tags=a",[393,1773,1774],{},"vld::array(vld::string())",[393,1776,1777],{},"[\"a\"]",[389,1779,1780,1781,1784,1785,818,1788,1784,1791,1794,1795,1798,1799,1802,1803,1806,1807,1151],{},"So a schema describes the real types (",[393,1782,1783],{},"vld::number().int()"," for ",[393,1786,1787],{},"?page=2",[393,1789,1790],{},"vld::boolean()",[393,1792,1793],{},"?active=true",") and string fields keep working when the text happens to look numeric. JSON bodies are ",[1196,1796,1797],{},"not"," coerced: ",[393,1800,1801],{},"{\"page\": \"2\"}"," fails ",[393,1804,1805],{},"vld::number()"," unless the schema calls ",[393,1808,1809],{},".coerce()",[1811,1812,1814],"h3",{"id":1813},"query-strings-and-forms","Query strings and forms",[1274,1816,1817,1832,1842,1855,1870],{},[1277,1818,1819,1820,1823,1824,1827,1828,1831],{},"Keys and values are form-decoded (",[393,1821,1822],{},"+"," is a space, ",[393,1825,1826],{},"%XX"," is decoded as UTF-8; invalid sequences become ",[393,1829,1830],{},"U+FFFD",").",[1277,1833,1834,1835,1838,1839,1151],{},"A repeated key becomes an array: ",[393,1836,1837],{},"?tag=a&tag=b"," → ",[393,1840,1841],{},"{\"tag\": [\"a\", \"b\"]}",[1277,1843,1844,1845,1848,1849,1838,1852,1151],{},"A key ending in ",[393,1846,1847],{},"[]"," is always an array: ",[393,1850,1851],{},"?tag[]=a",[393,1853,1854],{},"{\"tag\": [\"a\"]}",[1277,1856,1857,1858,618,1860,1863,1864,1867,1868,1151],{},"A key without ",[393,1859,432],{},[393,1861,1862],{},"?flag",") and an empty value (",[393,1865,1866],{},"?x=",") are ",[393,1869,1518],{},[1277,1871,1872],{},"Form bodies are parsed the same way and may have at most 1000 fields (more is a 422).",[1811,1874,1876],{"id":1875},"path-parameters","Path parameters",[389,1878,1879],{},"Path parameters are percent-decoded exactly once and coerced like query values. A route without parameters produces an empty object, so a schema whose fields are all optional still validates.",[1811,1881,599],{"id":1882},"headers",[1274,1884,1885,1903,1923],{},[1277,1886,1887,1888,1891,1892,1895,1896,1899,1900,1151],{},"Names are lowercased and ",[393,1889,1890],{},"-"," becomes ",[393,1893,1894],{},"_",": ",[393,1897,1898],{},"X-Request-Id"," is the field ",[393,1901,1902],{},"x_request_id",[1277,1904,1905,1911,1912,1915,1916,1919,1920,1151],{},[1196,1906,1907,1908,1910],{},"Header names that already contain ",[393,1909,1894],{}," are ignored."," Otherwise a client could send ",[393,1913,1914],{},"x_user: admin"," and fill the ",[393,1917,1918],{},"x_user"," field even behind a proxy that strips only ",[393,1921,1922],{},"X-User",[1277,1924,1925,1926,1929,1930,1151],{},"Repeated headers are joined with ",[393,1927,1928],{},"\", \""," before coercion. Non-UTF-8 bytes become ",[393,1931,1830],{},[1811,1933,602],{"id":1934},"cookies",[1274,1936,1937,1944,1955],{},[1277,1938,1939,1940,1943],{},"Every ",[393,1941,1942],{},"Cookie"," header is read (HTTP\u002F2 clients may send one header per cookie); they are joined before parsing.",[1277,1945,1946,618,1949,1838,1952,1954],{},[1196,1947,1948],{},"The first occurrence of a name wins",[393,1950,1951],{},"sid=a; sid=b",[393,1953,528],{},"). Browsers send the most specific cookie first; letting a later one win would allow cookie tossing from a sibling subdomain.",[1277,1956,1957,1958,1961,1962,1964,1965,1159,1968,1973,1974,1976],{},"Names are used as-is (a cookie ",[393,1959,1960],{},"session-id"," needs a field named ",[393,1963,1960],{},", map it with ",[393,1966,1967],{},"as \"session-id\"",[528,1969,1970],{"href":85},[393,1971,1972],{},"schema!","). Values are unquoted, percent-decoded (",[393,1975,1822],{}," is kept) and coerced.",[568,1978,1980],{"id":1979},"body-limits","Body limits",[389,1982,1983,1156,1985,1987,1988,1990,1991,618,1994,1997,1998,2001,2002,2004,2005,2007,2008,1156,2010,2012,2013,2016,2017,2020,2021,2023,2024,1151],{},[393,1984,515],{},[393,1986,640],{}," never buffer more than the limit; a larger body is ",[1196,1989,1209],{},". The default everywhere is ",[1196,1992,1993],{},"2 MiB",[393,1995,1996],{},"vld_web::common::DEFAULT_BODY_LIMIT",", the same as axum's ",[393,1999,2000],{},"DefaultBodyLimit","), regardless of the framework's own JSON default. ",[393,2003,156],{}," honours axum's ",[393,2006,2000],{},"; ",[393,2009,829],{},[393,2011,180],{}," honour Rocket ",[393,2014,2015],{},"limits"," \u002F Salvo ",[393,2018,2019],{},"secure_max_size",", but a value left at the framework's built-in default counts as unset and gives 2 MiB. Each framework page has a \"Body limit\" section with the setting to change it; ",[393,2022,192],{}," uses tonic's ",[393,2025,2026],{},"max_decoding_message_size",[389,2028,2029,2030,2032,2033,2036,2037,703,2039,2041,2042,2045],{},"Compressed request bodies: ",[393,2031,662],{}," decodes ",[393,2034,2035],{},"Content-Encoding"," itself (the limit applies to the decoded size), ",[393,2038,702],{},[393,2040,706],{}," do with the ",[393,2043,2044],{},"ntex-compress"," feature, the other modules see the body as the framework delivers it.",[568,2047,122],{"id":2048},"openapi",[389,2050,2051,2052,2060,2061,2069,2070,2075,2076,2081,2082,818,2085,818,2088,2091,2092,2096,2097,2099],{},"The modules only validate. To document the same schemas, use ",[528,2053,2054,703,2057],{"href":223},[393,2055,2056],{},"vld_openapi::utoipa5",[393,2058,2059],{},"utoipa6"," (framework-agnostic) or ",[528,2062,2063,703,2066],{"href":227},[393,2064,2065],{},"vld_openapi::schemars0",[393,2067,2068],{},"schemars1"," (also for aide); with poem-openapi, ",[528,2071,2072],{"href":231},[393,2073,2074],{},"vld_openapi::poem_openapi"," documents and validates in one step. loco-rs controllers use ",[528,2077,2078],{"href":213},[393,2079,2080],{},"vld_web::axum"," unchanged. The error body structs (",[393,2083,2084],{},"ValidationErrorBody",[393,2086,2087],{},"ErrorBody",[393,2089,2090],{},"ErrorWithMessage",") live in ",[528,2093,2094],{"href":197},[393,2095,196],{}," and are ",[393,2098,552],{}," types, so they can be registered as response schemas too.",[2101,2102,2103],"style",{},"html pre.shiki code .sMK4o, html code.shiki .sMK4o{--shiki-light:#39ADB5;--shiki-default:#89DDFF;--shiki-dark:#89DDFF}html pre.shiki code .sBMFI, html code.shiki .sBMFI{--shiki-light:#E2931D;--shiki-default:#FFCB6B;--shiki-dark:#FFCB6B}html pre.shiki code .sTEyZ, html code.shiki .sTEyZ{--shiki-light:#90A4AE;--shiki-default:#EEFFFF;--shiki-dark:#BABED8}html pre.shiki code .sfazB, html code.shiki .sfazB{--shiki-light:#91B859;--shiki-default:#C3E88D;--shiki-dark:#C3E88D}html .light .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-light);background: var(--shiki-light-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-light-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-light-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-light-text-decoration);}html.light .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-light);background: var(--shiki-light-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-light-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-light-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-light-text-decoration);}html .default .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-default);background: var(--shiki-default-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-default-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-default-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-default-text-decoration);}html .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-default);background: var(--shiki-default-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-defaul